{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Sign","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.transposition_not_in_sign_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.transposition_not_in_sign_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L139-L144","doc":"Corollary: a transposition is an odd permutation — it is not in the\nkernel of the sign homomorphism, so the sign-rep action is genuinely\nnontrivial (the antisymmetry is not vacuous). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.sign_transposition_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.sign_transposition_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L128-L137","doc":"**Open-work item (2), formalized.** Every transposition of three\ncolor labels acts on the sign representation of `S_3` as\nmultiplication by `-1`: the sign of `Equiv.swap i j` (for `i ≠ j`,\n`i j : Fin 3`) is `-1`. This is the representation-theoretic\ngenerator of the color antisymmetry posited by the\n`FermiColorSinglet` conjecture — proved directly from Mathlib's\nsign homomorphism, sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.fermi_implies_signWeight_eq_one_sixth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.fermi_implies_signWeight_eq_one_sixth","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L97-L106","doc":"**Conditional theorem**: if a baryon admits a Fermi color singlet\nstructure, then its sign-block Plancherel weight at H_3 = 1/6.\n\nTrivial corollary using the scaffold's data. Future work will\npromote this to a non-trivial statement once the substrate\ncolor machinery is in place. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet.color_in_sign_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet.color_in_sign_rep","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L93-L93","doc":"**Conjectural content (V_(1,1,1) sign rep).** The color action is\nantisymmetric — every transposition `Equiv.swap i j` (`i ≠ j`)\nnegates the color amplitude, i.e. the action carries the sign\ncharacter of `S_3`, placing the color state in the sign rep\n`V_(1,1,1)`. This is the substrate analogue of QCD color\nantisymmetry (Fermi statistics); the full categorical derivation\nis multi-session open work, so no instance is provided here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet.amplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet.amplitude","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The color amplitude that the action scales. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet.colorAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet.colorAction","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The baryon's color action: a permutation of the three color\nlabels acts on the (one-dimensional) color amplitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet.mk","kind":"ctor","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.FermiColorSinglet","kind":"class","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L63-L95","doc":"**Conjectural placeholder class**: substrate-level QCD color singlet.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond: this class axiomatizes the conjecture that\nthe proton (uud baryon) wave function on 3 color strands is fully\nantisymmetric (Fermi statistics), making the COLOR action lie in\nthe sign rep V_(1,1,1) of S_3.\n\nNO INSTANCE is provided — the class IS the conjecture. The full\ncategorical derivation requires multi-session substrate-level\nwork that does not yet exist (PR #1654 Item B reframing).\n\nFuture agents pursuing the derivation should:\n  1. Define the substrate analog of a \"color strand\"\n  2. Define the substrate analog of \"anti-symmetric under S_n action\"\n  3. Prove the proton's substrate representation is in this class\n\nNone of these are formalized yet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.signPlancherelWeight_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.signPlancherelWeight_3","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L57-L61","doc":"At H_3 (n=3), the sign rep Plancherel weight is 1/6 (matches\n`ProtonMassEMSignBlock.plancherelSignH3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.signPlancherelWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Substrate.ColorAntisymmetric.signPlancherelWeight","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Substrate/ColorAntisymmetric.lean#L52-L55","doc":"The Plancherel weight of the sign rep of S_n equals `1/n!`.\nSince the sign rep is 1-dimensional, `P_(sign) = 1²/n! = 1/n!`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}